<title>UK: Mexico sets $1.0 billion 10-year bond.</title>
<headline>Mexico sets $1.0 billion 10-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico on Wedneday launched a $1.0 billion 10-year bond which will be priced to yield around 337.5 basis points over U.S. Treasuries, joint lead managers Merrill Lynch and Salomon Brothers said. </p>
<p>The offering will be priced during Thursday's New York session. Other details were not immediately available.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
